From 177472ea791bcab130ca54caecae95adef7d9455 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:45:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 39/58] serve: STRATA_CONV_TIER_DIR=<folder> spills
 conversations the RAM cache evicts to disk, and reads them back

An emergency overflow below the conversation cache (conversation_tier.hpp, pure host code).  When make_room evicts a
conversation to make room for another, one of at least STRATA_CONV_TIER_MIN_TOKENS (16384) tokens goes to a writer
thread instead of being freed: one session file (format v1: O_DIRECT, temporary file, flush, rename) per stage of a
layer split, written at once, then a meta file as the commit record (tokens, checkpoint lengths, the run-time marks v1
does not hold: pinned, slot_turn, draftless).  A request whose prompt the tier holds STRATA_CONV_TIER_MIN_GAIN (2048)
more tokens of than the RAM cache, a slot or the live session reads it back (all stages at once, the per-stage read
limits, the RAM preflight) and validates it before anything is parked; an image still waiting for the writer is
handed back as it is.  Any failure (I/O, a corrupt or foreign file, RAM) reads the prompt instead.

- Only make_room's evictions spill: ConversationCache::evict_oldest(spill) and an eviction sink.  The RAM floor's and a
  save's evictions free the memory at once (counted as drops_ram); drop_superseded and clear() never reach the sink.
- Written once: an image a file holds all but fewer than STRATA_CONV_TIER_REGROW_TOKENS (8192) of, or an earlier copy
  of a conversation on disk, is not written again; grown further it is written in full and the older file set goes.
- STRATA_CONV_TIER_WRITE_GB_DAY (200 GB per local calendar day, kept in <folder>/budget), _CAP_GB (600), _MAX_FILES
  (2000), _TTL_H (168, by last use, LRU to the cap), _INFLIGHT_MIB (2048), _MIN_FREE_GB (64).
- Identity: the session identity mixed with the engine binary, its arguments and its STRATA_* environment.  An earlier
  run's files are removed at start unless STRATA_CONV_TIER_WARM=1 (then indexed; other identities kept to their TTL).
- STRATA_CONV_TIER_VERIFY=1: every write read back and compared with the evicted image; every restore checked against
  a digest of it.  #879 clears the tier too.
- Counters on every "conversation tier:" log line (files, disk bytes, written today, budget left, spills, restores,
  misses, drops by reason).  conversation_session_read_limits gets a draft-pointer overload.

Off (no env): byte-identical (bt16, il against the stage-1 dumps).  Forced on (one RAM slot, every eviction spilled,
verify): bt16, T=0.7, interleave byte-identical with 15/15/9 restores from disk; overlap PASS; conversation_tier_test
(107 checks: spill only on eviction, min size, write-once, budget and day, TTL and cap, queue and in-flight bound,
exact restore, identity, I/O faults, crash leftovers).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
